\title{ripr: Reverse Information Projection onto Finite Unions of Convex Sets}
\description{
Approximates the growth-rate optimal e-variable for a composite null hypothesis, in the sense of Grünwald, de Heide and Koolen (2024) \doi{10.1093/jrsssb/qkae011}, by computing the reverse information projection (RIPr) of a fixed alternative onto a null given by a finite union of convex subsets of the parameter space. The subsets may overlap and their union may not be convex, so the projection may be found by numerical methods. We provide optimisers that return mixing measures and their induced mixtures that approximate the RIPr. The approximations are just that, so the likelihood ratio is not necessarily an e-value; nevertheless, an e-variable can be built by deriving a certified upper bound on the worst-case null expectation and dividing the ratio through that constant, which may be computed via our branch-and-bound algorithms.
}
